<title>SINGAPORE: ADNOC awards diesel tender to Petco, cancels jet.</title>
<headline>ADNOC awards diesel tender to Petco, cancels jet.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC) sold by tender 75,000 tonnes of gas oil to Malaysian state trader Petco at around 25 cents per barrel above MidEast spot quotes of two publications, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 0.5-percent sulphur gas oil is for end-July lifting, on a free-on-board (fob) Ruwais basis.</p>
<p>The awarded price is lower than what Petco paid for ADNOC's previous gas oil cargo at 35 cents per barrel above MidEast spot quotes, for June 22-24 lifting, fob Ruwais.</p>
<p>Traders also said ADNOC has cancelled its tender to sell end-July jet fuel which also closed on June 25.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
